{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/582967-sell-me-on-changeling-the-dreaming","id":582967,"title":"Sell me on Changeling: The Dreaming","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-07-07T18:38:59-07:00","id":582967,"title":"Sell me on Changeling: The Dreaming","content":"Alright, I'll admit, I am a huge fan of Changeling: The Lost and was initially dismissive of Dreaming, but in all honesty, I have never read or played it and know next to nothing about it. Maybe I should give it a fair chance. I'm most familiar with Vampire and a little bit of Werewolf and Mage, (<span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Don't stir this pot again, you've been spoken to about it repeatedly and will be banned if you do so again. Darksider)</span> So, maybe it may be worth looking into, though I know very little of it.<br /> <br /> So, to all the Changeling: The Dreaming fans, tell me the merits of this game and why I would like it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","user":"Darksider","date":". 07-07-2015, 10:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-08T20:33:05-07:00","id":584111,"title":"","content":"Lesbian Elves. Wait, that's the webcomic Chrysalis. My bad.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Onyx Path Kickstarters I back.<br /> W20, MtC, CB20, DtD, MtAs20, BotW20, Wraith 20th.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1442-paladindemo","name":"PaladinDemo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1442_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"622"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T05:08:27-07:00","id":584532,"title":"","content":"Why not buy the book, read it, and play it?<br /> <br /> Here's the game I run online (most recently we invited mages to join too): <a href=\"http://rpol.net/game.cgi?gi=63447\" target=\"_blank\">http://rpol.net/game.cgi?gi=63447</a><br /> <br /> Take a look around and get a feel for the flavour.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T09:51:56-07:00","id":584844,"title":"","content":"Who doesn't like roleplaying an extended puberty metaphor?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T12:52:37-07:00","id":585046,"title":"","content":"I'm sure there are people that don't.<br /> <br /> But I'm not really sure &quot;extended puberty metaphor&quot; is a good sell for CtD. For most people, puberty is about the difficulties of growing up with the rewards of life getting better on the other side via importantly cultural milestones, and increased social independence/power. CtD's themes that focus on the idea of &quot;growing up is bad&quot; run counter to a puberty metaphor, because instead of an emotionally trying time that you hope leads to greater possibilities, adventures, and self-expression once you make it through, the game says growing up does the exact opposite as it starts to limit you.<br /> <br /> I'd kind of push the metaphor into more of the transition from college to full social adulthood rather than puberty.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T15:24:42-07:00","id":585284,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/582967-sell-me-on-changeling-the-dreaming?p=584844#post584844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Who doesn't like roleplaying an extended puberty metaphor?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's overly simplistic. Like saying 'who doesn't like playing an extended metaphor of high school angst' for Vampire.<br /> <br /> It's an urban fantasy setting with magic, politics and adventure. You can run a variety of themes - puberty metaphors aren't essential ;-)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-11T23:23:04-07:00","id":587835,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/582967-sell-me-on-changeling-the-dreaming?p=584532#post584532\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why not buy the book, read it, and play it?<br /> <br /> Here's the game I run online (most recently we invited mages to join too): <a href=\"http://rpol.net/game.cgi?gi=63447\" target=\"_blank\">http://rpol.net/game.cgi?gi=63447</a><br /> <br /> Take a look around and get a feel for the flavour.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dammit. I got a Son of Ether who proudly proclaims &quot;I brought Science bitches!&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Onyx Path Kickstarters I back.<br /> W20, MtC, CB20, DtD, MtAs20, BotW20, Wraith 20th.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1442-paladindemo","name":"PaladinDemo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1442_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"622"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-12T00:39:51-07:00","id":587906,"title":"","content":"A Sons of Ether character would probably get on well with the nockers. Plus, our game specifically has magick with a scientific edge in it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-12T00:49:39-07:00","id":587914,"title":"","content":"The very first thing to say is: forget Changeling: The Lost.<br /> <br /> It doesn't have anything to do with The Lost being worse. It does have to do with both being completely different games.<br /> <br /> Dreaming is about Living Dreams trying to saty around in the nihilistic setting of the Classic WoD. Your character is a fae that had long ago to go through The Changeling Way, a powerful spell that made you reincarnate on a human body to protect you from Banality, the anti-dream stuff that fills the world each passing day. You're almost immortal if you avoid cold iron, bringing old memories to each new life, but still have to deal with your human body.<br /> <br /> As a common theme, is a game about balancing wonder and pragmatism, with the risk of madness if any side takes too much from you. Is about learning to grow when you're a child (because the game is MADE to support child characters), and remembering to stay a little childish when you grow up, so you never let the banality of life take the wonder that gives it sense.<br /> <br /> From there, a lot of interesting and very diverse stories can come.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-12T02:18:11-07:00","id":587972,"title":"","content":"Childish in the sense of 'imaginative, open-minded and full of play', rather than 'petty, mean and immature', of course. Maybe child-like is a better term, actually.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-12T02:34:49-07:00","id":587977,"title":"","content":"Why the separation?<br /> <br /> Unseelie changelings don't really work if they can't be petty, mean, and immature.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-12T06:26:33-07:00","id":588082,"title":"","content":"Well that was one of my big bugbears with the fluff: the Unseelie legacies were pretty one dimensional in a way Nature/Demeanor aren't. Unseelie can be individualist, dogmatic and perverse, sure. But I wouldn't describe them as childish.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-12T09:01:45-07:00","id":588196,"title":"","content":"I wasn't trying to say all Unseelie are childish, just that both ways of view the word apply to the original statement just fine because of the Seelie/Unseelie split.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-12T10:01:57-07:00","id":588253,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/582967-sell-me-on-changeling-the-dreaming?p=587906#post587906\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Sons of Ether character would probably get on well with the nockers. Plus, our game specifically has magick with a scientific edge in it.</div> </div> </div> </div>My Etherite uses a Nintendo Zapper as a weapon, and created an anti-magic field generator, which also works on the Technocracy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Onyx Path Kickstarters I back.<br /> W20, MtC, CB20, DtD, MtAs20, BotW20, Wraith 20th.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1442-paladindemo","name":"PaladinDemo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1442_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"622"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-12T17:01:21-07:00","id":588587,"title":"","content":"The best way I can try to describe/sell it is that it starts out a bit like the main character in Hook, trying to rediscover the things that made him both happy and that long lost and forgotten aspect of himself that many others but him/herself can still see glimpses of. After that, or at least the early road of that, it begins to shift into a (more fantastical than technological version of the Matrix combined with some other aspects of maybe Hellboy. Both kind of walk in two separate, but partially linked worlds where a lot of others are either out to get them or to destroy/corrupt what aspects they need to exist. Another sort of way to look at it is vaguely similar to nWoD's Geist the Sin-Eater. But only vaguely.<br /> <br /> A lot of the issues with CtD is that it is so hard to get into and to take seriously as a game. I don't mean this to be insulting. But it really kind of goes a long way away from basically every other WoD game there is, and that is basically what killed it. It's very difficult to be compatible with the rest of the WoD. It really dives into the pre-teen and teen angst, but also is supposed to be a mature (and I mean mentality here, not pornography) game, too, which are two very different themes to push.<br /> <br /> It doesn't help that they are also, generally speaking, not a very scary &quot;monster&quot;, but also pretty dang close to &quot;superheroes&quot;, struggling against well, natural forces that in a lot of ways most people either embrace or accept to a certain extend as a good thing, and is only really something bad to them. Again, it's kind of difficult to take them that seriously in that respect.<br /> <br /> Similar to VtM and WtA, there is a certain level of political tension as well between the courts, but in all honesty, even amongst a lot of CtD fans, the material is not terribly well explained.If this would have been much the main focus and delved into a lot more deeply, I think the game might have done a lot better. Basically, you have two big groups with the same goal, but different methods and beliefs about how to achieve them, which are not mutually exclusive. Unfortunately, it kind of seems that the setting as a whole favored the lighter, nobler group over the darker, scarier one, and it really undercut both the whole deal with the political factions and the Unseelie as a whole.<br /> <br /> A lot of the issue with the game is that, well, ok, Vampires have their nightly struggle against the Beast and the eternal struggle for power and position. Werewolves, a bit closer to Changlings, also fight a huge ongoing war against primal powers. But for t Garou, it's an epic battle that they have basically already lost. Now, they just want to defend as much as they can for as long as they can and go down fighting. Not so much for the Kith. They &quot;fight&quot; a sort of psychological war against the, um, lack of creativity. The more they &quot;loose&quot;, the more people go see a movie instead of write a book. The more they play a video game instead of painting a picture. The more they develop voice amplifying and altering software instead of singing a song. Well, that's pretty true, but it's also a bit of an oversimplification. It also means a lot of the creatures, beings, places, spirits, etc. . . that have been created &quot;from the Dreaming&quot; cease to exist more and more. That's why, for example, real dragons basically don't exist any more. Well, they do in the Dreaming, the sort of secret Faery world. Sort of like the Matrix, but Neo the Faerie sort of exist in the Dreaming (Matrix) and the real world at the same time. If you are familiar with it, it's similar to the Maxx in a way. The more that Banality (not-creativity) grow and grow, that is the sort of thing that Changlings all &quot;fight&quot; against, (but it's not an actual thing like the Wyrm, Technocracy, or Antediluvians, that is, you can't actually go out and fight it), the more one of their worlds shrinks and dies, and the less of the energy they sort of feed upon there is to go around.<br /> <br /> Changlings also have access to certain magical abilities, and the best way I can kind of describe it is kind of like the Norse myth of Baldur and Loki. Where they went around and made a deal with everything in existence to not hurt Baldur, except they forgot to talk to Mistletoe, and someone throws a Mistletoe dart and it kills Baldur. That's kind of how their magic works. They made a pact with something/someone to be able to do certain things. Kind of brief, but that's the basic idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://t0.gstatic.com/images?q=tbn:ANd9GcTAO8runv-CR5dodCXgw_8wdJype5yunYCODWdZiBAwUP5WFVv8\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://ksr-ugc.imgix.net/assets/003/593/392/92a29c2836b988505781770a32720148_original.png?v=1428699067&amp;w=700&amp;h=&amp;fit=max&amp;auto=format&amp;lossless=true&amp;s=69ffdde357a0cdd88ee89934622443f9\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1721-beckett","name":"Beckett","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1721_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1077"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-12T19:28:21-07:00","id":588734,"title":"","content":"In a sense, Changeling is about living in the World of Darkness when you're NOTHING like it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-12T20:32:11-07:00","id":588800,"title":"","content":"Okay, in a lot ways, Changeling is about standing your ground and refusing to let the world roll over you. Its about being unique and looking at the world in way that few others can. the world around you is saying &quot;this is the way the world is.&quot; and you're all like: &quot;But its so much better this way.&quot; its about being inspired so much that you make the world a little more wonderful all the while everyone around you refuses to believe its even possible. it's about finding beauty in the mundane and stability in the fantastic. it's about grabbing on your passion with both hands as the cold and dreary world around you freeze your fingers black and turn your tears to ice. it's about being so scared you feel alive and so entranced by beauty your heart breaks. Changeling is about remembering who you were and the excitement of who you can become if only you can break the chains of &quot;impossible&quot;. <br /> <br /> Changeling is about <i><b>LIFE</b></i> when surrounded by death and the soul crushing despair of merely surviving. its about looking at the world and saying: &quot;You haven't broken me yet.&quot; the rest is just window dressing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5767-deedee","name":"DeeDee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"116"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-22T03:32:09-07:00","id":599153,"title":"","content":"One nice thing about <b>Changeling </b>is that you can play around with ideas that just don't fit elsewhere in the World of Darkness (and which you wouldn't want spilling over into other parts of the setting). Changelings build with dreams, their equivalent to nodes/caerns/etc. are places where human dreams can manifest in tangible form (for them, at least). So the sky's really the limit.<br /> <br /> Any sort of &quot;pocket dimension&quot; or &quot;private world&quot; works wonderfully with <i>Changeling. </i>Willy Wonka's chocolate factory, Silent Hill, Narnia or Neverland . . .any sort of story where a place of magic and wonder exists alongside &quot;normalcy&quot;, which ordinary people can't reach. Changelings, like small kids, know that a hop, skip, and a jump can sometimes take you &quot;under hill&quot; or through the looking glass.<br /> <br /> Want to visit Camp Crystal Lake (<i>Friday the 13th</i>) or Grendel's mere (<i>Beowulf</i>)? You're talking about Graymere Glen, a freehold in Connecticut. Where the willows walk, and only a fool swims in the lake.<br /> <br /> Feel like going steampunk for a bit? Consider visiting Goblin Town, a giant clockwork town/machine built under New York City.<br /> <br /> Want to sing &quot;Let It Go&quot; in Elsa's ice palace (from <i>Frozen)</i>? Or maybe play a friendly game of croquet in Alice's Wonderland? How about skipping through the Emerald City (which is perfect for a Seattle based game)? A changeling can visit any of those places - and drag their friends from the other game lines along for the ride (the Jabberwocky vs. an elder Tzimisce should be loads of fun to watch).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/582967-sell-me-on-changeling-the-dreaming?p=588734#post588734\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In a sense, Changeling is about living in the World of Darkness when you're NOTHING like it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Building on that idea - you could argue that <b>Changeling </b>is about LARPing in the World of Darkness . . . except that its all real - and your in-game actions have real consequences. The &quot;prop&quot; gun really does fire. The &quot;imaginary&quot; dragon <i>can</i> set a building on fire. You really are a fairy princess, or knight on a white horse . ..<br /> <br /> . . . at least until Banality takes you, and you forget that any of it ever happened.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4624,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","user":"One Vorlon","date":". 07-22-2015, 06:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-22T05:53:07-07:00","id":599272,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Camilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/582967-sell-me-on-changeling-the-dreaming#post582967\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alright, I'll admit, I am a huge fan of Changeling: The Lost and was initially dismissive of Dreaming, but in all honesty, I have never read or played it and know next to nothing about it. Maybe I should give it a fair chance. I'm most familiar with Vampire and a little bit of Werewolf and Mage, (<span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Don't stir this pot again, you've been spoken to about it repeatedly and will be banned if you do so again. Darksider)</span> So, maybe it may be worth looking into, though I know very little of it.<br /> <br /> So, to all the Changeling: The Dreaming fans, tell me the merits of this game and why I would like it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Right well I watched a video of somebody read through the Dreaming's core book and here is <b>my abridged version</b> of its premise and backstory.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Thanks to the mages being greedy pricks, they practically killed humanity's ability to believe in the supernatural. This caused magic and imagination to dwindle in human society. The Fae are creatures born of imagination and dreams, so they slowly began to die off. In an effort to survive, the nobility fled back to the world of the Fae, abandoning the peasantry to the human world as they shut and locked the doors behind him.<br /> <br /> The peasants found a way to survive though, by merging themselves with human hosts, thus becoming the first Changelings. They struggled to rekindle humanity's imagination and wonder alive because that is what sustains them. A Changeling who loses their belief in magic and dreams either becomes a full human or they simply die.<br /> <br /> <br /> In the modern era, the mages orchestrated the moon landing in an effort to prove to humanity that there were no supernatural horrors living there and thus give the mages a chance to construct a base of operations <b>on the fucking moon</b>, which backfired tremendously for them. For a brief moment all over the world, humanity believed they were capable of anything, and this belief was strong enough to blow the doors open to the Fae realm and the long isolated nobles came flooding back into the world. But unlike the peasantry who had survived for centuries now without a monarchy system, the nobles still believed they should rule by default, and so they began demanding the peasants hand over all their land and valuables and get on their knees once more.<br /> <br /> <br /> Naturally the peasants fought back, and with the nobles being centuries out of touch with the world, the peasants had the upper hand. Cities were practically overrun with iron constructs. If they wanted to survive, the nobles had to adapt, and so they became Changelings as well. The nobility are called the Sidhe (pronounced She) and while they primarily rule Changeling society now, they have begrudgingly allowed the peasants to join their noble households, provided that they prove themselves worthy of it.<br /> <br /> <br /> The story of Dreaming is, as mentioned in an earlier post, an extended puberty story. Your character starts off with all these cool powers derived from dreams and emotions, but as you grow older and the human world has bigger expectations for you, you slowly corrode. It is rare for a Changeling to survive past adulthood without suffering complete banality, which means most Changelings are either children or teenagers.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=YjhSziyvODM\" target=\"_blank\">Here's the video if you want a more thorough introduction to Dreaming.</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 07-22-2015, 09:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-22T06:10:56-07:00","id":599287,"title":"","content":"Just to remember, not every Changeling slumber or dies with Banality.<br /> <br /> There's allways Dawntain, the Autumn People, using the power of the Dreaming to KILL it...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-22T09:42:15-07:00","id":599538,"title":"","content":"By mages, I hope you mean &quot;the Order of Reason&quot; and the &quot;Technocratic Union&quot; because it's hard to see all the other mages doing all the fantastic things as being banal at all. In fact, it's a really weird dichotomy in Changeling, not Mage, that all the fervent dreams of TECHNOCRATIC mages are what put humans on the Moon. And, then, later, put getting some normal mundane humans onto the Moon on TV (another one of those technocratic inventions that spreads dreams all over the place.) And then they have Technocrats be banal. While Knockers aren't. <br /> <br /> Mages are humans who can make their dreams real. Changelings are real dreams. Characterizing the relationship this way is a little off base. Dreams are dreams. The Union just wants you to dream THEIR dreams because they are safer dreams for humans that put humans first. But inside those bounds, go for it. It's like writing a sonnet vs. free verse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-22T10:17:57-07:00","id":599602,"title":"","content":"If you look at the (very suspect) Banality chart... mages actually all rank fairly high considering what they do. Sure Technocrats are the worst, but a Virtual Adept or Hermetic aren't much better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-22T16:33:31-07:00","id":599964,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/582967-sell-me-on-changeling-the-dreaming?p=599602#post599602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you look at the (very suspect) Banality chart... mages actually all rank fairly high considering what they do. Sure Technocrats are the worst, but a Virtual Adept or Hermetic aren't much better.</div> </div> </div> </div> Confusingly, there are two different places you can get this info in the core book. p.287 has them at 5-7 (8-10 for Technocrats). On p.281, the ratings differ: mysticks are 2-4, true believers are 4-6 and modern cynics are 6-8. I opt for the ratings on p.281.<br /> <br /> Banality is tied to patterns and repetition. That's why the Technocrats are so Banal. Their paradigm is also oppressive and doesn't have room for other paradigms. These things crush the Dreaming. True, there are Enlightened folks in the Technocracy, but the majority of its members are not encouraged to think. Only the privileged few.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-22T17:47:27-07:00","id":600010,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/582967-sell-me-on-changeling-the-dreaming?p=599964#post599964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Banality is tied to patterns and repetition. That's why the Technocrats are so Banal. Their paradigm is also oppressive and doesn't have room for other paradigms. These things crush the Dreaming. True, there are Enlightened folks in the Technocracy, but the majority of its members are not encouraged to think. Only the privileged few.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Union definitely wants people to have issues with changelings. After all, changelings are extra-dimensional entities that infest human hosts of a specific genetic type and co-opt their hosts entire existence to their own ends (like those caterpillars that turn ladybugs into living zombies). And those ends are effectively much like pushing drugs and then acting like psychic vampires (at best) or operating in ways that are as appalling as vampires and werewolves- hunting humans for sport, eating them, etc. (at worst). <br /> <br /> The Union definitely wants people to conform to specific lifestyle, admittedly one that's pretty sweet compared to that of the Middle Ages. Unless you demonstrate the level Enlightenment needed to change from one of the Watched Over to one of the Watchers. <br /> <br /> Those viewpoints are effectively pretty banal, but, in many ways, completely understandable.<br /> <br /> But the Union is also responsible for the Moon landing. And the reaction that set off is not an accident. That was straight from the pure unbridled creative juices of the Union. The Union WANTED people to be inspired by the Moon landing. It suits their ends, makes their view of the destiny of humanity more real. And that incidentally opened the way from Arcadia to Earth. So, it was actually the banal Technocracy that vitalized Changeling society from the furtive and fading Commoner Freeholds to the Grand Pagentry of the modern kingdoms. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-22T20:08:41-07:00","id":600138,"title":"","content":"In the end, the Technoracy just got a high Banality rate to keep with their role of &quot;MiB-style villains&quot;.<br /> <br /> Considering what really are out there about them, I dare to say that an Enlightened Agent is probably as banal as any other mage. And that should be a pretty low Banality rate. I'm more inclined to alocate high Banality to a Hermetic than to a Void Engineer.<br /> <br /> Even some sleeper agents of the Union could be low Banality. They are used to technological wonders, and to dream of the future the Union can bring on Earth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-24T17:29:06-07:00","id":602384,"title":"","content":"Only the Technocracy could make flying to the moon routine. That's their contradiction. They created a moment of wonder to ultimately tame the unknown. In doing so, and in repeating the space flight thing multiple times, they actually reduced the wonder of it, arguably.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-24T18:30:32-07:00","id":602409,"title":"","content":"I think it is like the great explorations era. Explorators did outstanding things, go to places where no one was before, or places of forgotten civilizations. It was wondrous and exciting. However, in the long run, the world became smaller and great a amount of &quot;magic&quot; in travelling and distant places are somewhat lost. No more &quot;there be dragons&quot; on the maps. We know almost every corner of the earth and there is civilization almost everywhere. Now, I'm not saying it is inherently bad. It is always about the contradiction between the wonder of exploration and the wonder of the unexplored itself. Or, when we speak about the Technocracy, between safety and freedom. Or confromism and cretaivity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-24T21:22:38-07:00","id":602542,"title":"","content":"But again, that isn't a technocratic game, its the game of all Mages. They repeat the process to bring it to the Consensus. In no instance the Technocracy want people not to wonder, they love when people are amazed with science. What they want is that people believe enough for that to be real in the Consensus.<br /> <br /> And EVERY Mage wants that. Some just for power, others for ideological reasons.<br /> <br /> The Technocratic Union's Mages are wonderworkers as every other Mages. They do the impossible, like ray guns, levitation pods, teleporters, telepatic scanners, giant-robot-dinosaurs! A Hitmark V is a thing brought right from Terminator, and Authoctonia puts the Death Star to shame. Doesn't matter how much their organization helped to bring Banality unto the world (and it happened but not in such straightforward manner), you can't say those PEOPLE are high Banality.<br /> <br /> You could argue at most that they cultivate high Banality Sleepers to use against Changelings. They already do it for use against Mages, but they suffer to work their thing near these people as much as any Tradition Mage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-25T22:37:02-07:00","id":603512,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/582967-sell-me-on-changeling-the-dreaming?p=602384#post602384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Only the Technocracy could make flying to the moon routine. That's their contradiction. They created a moment of wonder to ultimately tame the unknown. In doing so, and in repeating the space flight thing multiple times, they actually reduced the wonder of it, arguably.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's part of what makes the Technocracy so toxic to Changelings. When miracles cease to be seen as miraculous, and become as common as sliced bread, they stop inspiring people. Which makes them &quot;dead&quot; to changelings.<br /> <br /> Changelings need people to be impressed, shocked, awed. Jolted out of their ruts, they dream about the impossible . . . and produce the Glamour changelings so desperately need. The moon landing hit every human on the planet. For a moment, even the most banal, close-minded Autumn Person watched in amazement as men walked on another world . . . and anything seemed possible. Five billion human souls producing Glamour, and not a one producing Banality - its a wonder the very walls of Arcadia weren't torn asunder by such a tsunami.<br /> <br /> But now, when space flights are so mundane, they no longer make the paper . . . The first time a song is played, its a goldmine of Glamour. But once it goes multi-platinum, everyone gets sick of it, and its been turned into elevator music . . . its pretty worthless to them.<br /> <br /> (Incidentally, that may well mean that certain changelings are hoarding potentially world-changing art/books/music, keeping them hidden away, only allowing a few humans each year to experience them . . .and experience 'em only once, to preserve their Glamour potential. Even if that means the creators starve in poverty, or die believing their works to be failures) <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-26T02:46:32-07:00","id":603695,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure that's a good case to justify the Technocracy as inherently banal. It's blaming basic human nature on them.<br /> <br /> The Technocracy pumps out &quot;miracles&quot; even if not on the Glamour-generating-level as the moon landing all the time. But the same thing happens, as always happens with humans, and new and amazing turns into mundane and ordinary.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-26T05:43:10-07:00","id":603757,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/582967-sell-me-on-changeling-the-dreaming?p=603695#post603695\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure that's a good case to justify the Technocracy as inherently banal. It's blaming basic human nature on them.<br /> <br /> The Technocracy pumps out &quot;miracles&quot; even if not on the Glamour-generating-level as the moon landing all the time. But the same thing happens, as always happens with humans, and new and amazing turns into mundane and ordinary.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you're all forgetting the Technocracy's underlying motivations, though: for the most part, they DON'T want people to think. The Technocracy is about controlling people and dominating the consensus. The only free will is for the Enlightened.<br /> <br /> They may have had noble origins in the beginning, but they've always represented humanity's worst tendencies to oppress in the name of progress.<br /> <br /> It's about more than rote and ritual making things less wonderful. Those things are inherent to humanity, as you say. It's more about making things mundane so that they become the ONLY way the world works.<br /> <br /> The Dreaming is about potential, dynamism and things that don't make sense. As an organisation that ultimately tries to make everything make sense, and on their terms, the Technocracy is the exact opposite of the Dreaming. The Dreaming tells you there might be monsters under your bed, while the Technocracy not only shows you there isn't but proves to you why you were wrong and silly to be scared in the first place (literally killing the dream of the monster under the bed).<br /> <br /> To return to the space travel analogy, they made it mundane not so that we could all fly among the stars but so that we could only ever fly into space on their terms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":5291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","user":"adambeyoncelowe","date":". 07-26-2015, 08:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-26T12:47:37-07:00","id":604031,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/582967-sell-me-on-changeling-the-dreaming?p=603757#post603757\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you're all forgetting the Technocracy's underlying motivations, though: for the most part, they DON'T want people to think. The Technocracy is about controlling people and dominating the consensus. The only free will is for the Enlightened.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well... no. I'm just responding to a specific point. Not making a overarching statement.<br /> <br /> The Technocracy doesn't have a motivation. Besides the multiple different canonical versions of the Technocracy, it's an organization of people. Different factions in the Union have different motivations, goals, and philosophies. It's not actually a monolithic organization with a single hive mind. Banality is a personal issue. Belonging to an organization with Banal tendencies doesn't mean you can't be creative and encouraging of creativity.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Dreaming is about potential, dynamism and things that don't make sense. </div> </div> </div>It's also worth remembering the Dreaming isn't &quot;good.&quot; Dreams of the negative aspects of reality are just as much a part of it as the positive parts. It's a thing of nightmares as well as fantasies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-26T16:24:39-07:00","id":604285,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/582967-sell-me-on-changeling-the-dreaming?p=604031#post604031\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well... no. I'm just responding to a specific point. Not making a overarching statement.<br /> <br /> The Technocracy doesn't have a motivation. Besides the multiple different canonical versions of the Technocracy, it's an organization of people. Different factions in the Union have different motivations, goals, and philosophies. It's not actually a monolithic organization with a single hive mind. Banality is a personal issue. Belonging to an organization with Banal tendencies doesn't mean you can't be creative and encouraging of creativity.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> It's also worth remembering the Dreaming isn't &quot;good.&quot; Dreams of the negative aspects of reality are just as much a part of it as the positive parts. It's a thing of nightmares as well as fantasies.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wasn't specifically responding to you, but the point you and others had made.<br /> <br /> oWoD is pretty much written from the viewpoint of individuals sticking it to the man (in this case monoliths like the Tehnocracy) and resisting an oppressive status quo. The nuance came in relatively late. The whole Gothic-Punk thing is about that.<br /> <br /> I agree with you that not every Technocrat is banal, but the overall effect of the Technocracy as an organisation is one of Banality, as the rules say. Organisations should be judged on their overall effect, because otherwise they're not an organisation but individuals.<br /> <br /> You're arguing (presumably) that Technocrats shouldn't be inherently banal, and I'm pointing out why, in the RAW, they are and should be. It does make sense that they have higher Banality ratings in general by the criteria the writers use to measure these things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":5291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","user":"adambeyoncelowe","date":". 07-26-2015, 07:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-26T17:55:17-07:00","id":604365,"title":"","content":"I still don't buy it.<br /> <br /> Nothing against the idea of the Technocracy as an organization being a highly Banal org. But Banality Rating is an INDIVIDUAL thing, so it bears not so much resemblance to the overall effect of the organization in the outside world, but its effect in the inside.<br /> <br /> The ratings on the Changeling book are based on the initial concept of them, and it is fairly accurate since they where just thought as MiBs. But as the game developed, the Technocratic Union evolved like everything else, and isn't fair to deny them that. In the moment they where shown from the inside, what we saw was an organization of Mages like every other.<br /> <br /> Surely, the Technocracy wants a world of Stasis (in truth this statement is wrong, but lets stick to it). But its members AREN'T static people. They are Enlightened Scientists bringing to the world what should be impossible and making it possible. They strive to control the Consensus, but it is also so the marvels produced in their labs one day can be produced outside.<br /> <br /> As people, they are Mages like any other, marveling at the mysteries of the cosmos and never setling with what they have, going beyond even if only for heir own amusement. As an artist whose work never was made known to the public can still be low banality, so are the Technocrats.<br /> <br /> Because Banality isn't about organizational objectives. Its about people believing. And a Mage believe.<br /> <br /> <br /> Of course, it doesn't means the Union shouldn't be viewed as a potential threat, they surely are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-26T18:41:33-07:00","id":604381,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/582967-sell-me-on-changeling-the-dreaming?p=604285#post604285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wasn't specifically responding to you, but the point you and others had made.</div> </div> </div> </div>You... directly quoted me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The nuance came in relatively late. </div> </div> </div>That's... not entirely true. Mage was well into the first run of Convention books by the time Changeling 2e came out. Sorcerer's Crusade came out one year after Changeling 2e core, and the Guide to the Technocracy a year after that.<br /> <br /> This really has less to do with when these details started to emerge in the setting, but a lack of communication between the game lines as they were being written.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It does make sense that they have higher Banality ratings in general by the criteria the writers use to measure these things. </div> </div> </div>Making sense is hard when the books don't provide a consistent explanation of what makes something have a higher Banality rating. The books are exceedingly unclear about what they want Banality to represent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-27T06:07:06-07:00","id":604632,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/582967-sell-me-on-changeling-the-dreaming?p=604381#post604381\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You... directly quoted me.</div> </div> </div> </div>I did. Sorry. You were just the last person to say the Technocracy shouldn't be banal because of whatever. I think as an organisation, though, the Technocracy should be banal, even if individual members aren't. But I meant I wasn't specifically <i>just</i> disagreeing with you. In Britain we have a weird way of apologising for disagreeing with people by starting along the lines of, 'I'm not just disagreeing with you...' to make it clear our disagreements aren't personal. I'm not sure if this translates that well? I wasn't very clear.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This really has less to do with when these details started to emerge in the setting, but a lack of communication between the game lines as they were being written. </div> </div> </div>This is true, and that table in the book is written from a CTD perspective, not a Mage one. If I were playing a Mage game where Banality became an issue, I'd use a much more nuanced system for allocating individual Banality ratings.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Making sense is hard when the books don't provide a consistent explanation of what makes something have a higher Banality rating. The books are exceedingly unclear about what they want Banality to represent. </div> </div> </div>This is also true, and I wouldn't disagree here. Banality has been described differently in different sourcebooks and most CTD players regularly state that they'd like a clearer, functional definition that is more nuanced than 'magic good, science bad' (which, incidentally, can be seen as the original duality between Traditions/Technocracy in MTA too).<br /> <br /> I think it's best to see the Dreaming as the last manifestation of the Mythic in the human consciousness. The Technocracy played a huge part in the end of the Mythic Age, and as such, that's why they're anathema. The Dreaming is full of wonder, but the 'logic' of the Dreaming is one of the Mythic (fairytales, legends, oaths, quests, etc). The 'logic' of the Technocratic paradigm (and yes, I understand there are several, but let's say the 'official' paradigm of the organisation as a whole) is very un-Mythic, even if it can inspire wonder. It's rational, and imperial in a scientific and cultural sense. The Dreaming is the right brain, and the Technocracy is the left brain. They see things differently, even if they sometimes come up with the same results.<br /> <br /> So, for the purposes of brevity, I think it's fine that the table in CTD lists the Technocrats as 8-10 Banality. But for individual characters, obviously this will fluctuate.<br /> <br /> I would probably use Resonance here. Static Resonances would make the character more banal, while Dynamic Resonances would make the character less banal. Stasis (Weaver) is often linked to Banality, while Dynamism (Wyld) is linked to the Dreaming. In MTA, Technocrats are considered the more Static group, while Marauders are considered the more Dynamic. Hence, Technocrats are at the top of the Banality chart, while Marauders are at the bottom, and Mysticks fill the gaps in between.<br /> <br /> You have to remember that most adult humans have Banality 7 anyway, so the range for mages isn't really that shocking. Changelings are basically interacting with a world of make-believe that most adults simply won't believe is real.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-27T10:26:10-07:00","id":604799,"title":"","content":"It's a bit worse than that, if you think about it. The technocratic paradigm most likely includes &quot;there's no such thing as fairies&quot;, so it's not just that they don't <i>believe</i> in them. It's that around a technocrat it <i>actually starts being true. </i>I think it makes sense for that to cause banality regardless of whether or not the individual is the sort that normally would.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-27T17:09:38-07:00","id":605132,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/582967-sell-me-on-changeling-the-dreaming?p=604799#post604799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's a bit worse than that, if you think about it. The technocratic paradigm most likely includes &quot;there's no such thing as fairies&quot;, so it's not just that they don't <i>believe</i> in them. It's that around a technocrat it <i>actually starts being true. </i>I think it makes sense for that to cause banality regardless of whether or not the individual is the sort that normally would.</div> </div> </div> </div>That too. You said it more succinctly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-27T22:06:02-07:00","id":605296,"title":"","content":"Well, put that way makes a lot more sense.<br /> <br /> Personaly, I still like the premisse of Glamour vs Banality being Wonder vs Tedium. And by that, I wouldn't put the common ratings of Technocrats so high.<br /> <br /> A case could be done for the Paradigm question. Usualy Paradigm doesn't have this kind of effect upon supernaturals, but being sensible to Banality means you could easily consider Changelings sensible to Paradigm. But I would prefer to let that to a more pronounced effect: a Marauder of static Quiet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-28T02:18:50-07:00","id":605420,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/582967-sell-me-on-changeling-the-dreaming?p=605296#post605296\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, put that way makes a lot more sense.<br /> <br /> Personaly, I still like the premisse of Glamour vs Banality being Wonder vs Tedium. And by that, I wouldn't put the common ratings of Technocrats so high.<br /> <br /> A case could be done for the Paradigm question. Usualy Paradigm doesn't have this kind of effect upon supernaturals, but being sensible to Banality means you could easily consider Changelings sensible to Paradigm. But I would prefer to let that to a more pronounced effect: a Marauder of static Quiet.</div> </div> </div> </div>As Heavy Arms pointed out, part of the problem here is the definition(s) of Banality in the RAW. It is tedium, but it's also anti-(mythic) magic. It actually encompasses lots of things and is, by its nature, an abstraction. <br /> <br /> I'm just sore that we never got The Book of Glamour. That could've clarified so much.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-28T02:45:02-07:00","id":605426,"title":"","content":"That's something to wish for C20, if it ever happens.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-28T08:21:05-07:00","id":605618,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/582967-sell-me-on-changeling-the-dreaming?p=605426#post605426\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's something to wish for C20, if it ever happens.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The kickstarter is scheduled for fall 2015. In case you didn't know <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/schedule/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://theonyxpath.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/11/OPP-Metal.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/schedule/\" target=\"_blank\"> Current Projects &ndash; Onyx Path Publishing </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/schedule/\" target=\"_blank\"> http://theonyxpath.com/schedule/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-28T09:47:04-07:00","id":605662,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/582967-sell-me-on-changeling-the-dreaming?p=605426#post605426\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's something to wish for C20, if it ever happens.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have it on good authority that the first drafts are being written now <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> As for Book of Glamour, I would have loved to see it appear years ago! It was supposed to be a book that brought Changeling up to Revised era standards without actually publishing a new edition of the core book. Now, however, we're close to having an <b>actual</b> new edition of the core book. Finishing and releasing Book of Glamour along with the new core book seems like it would both a waste of effort and a step back for the game line.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"Poo